DEFAULT_ROLE alone enables SELECT and selects the role on login
CREATE USER without GRANT cannot implicitly grant account_admin
ALTER cannot select an ungranted role
An unchanged default still requires ALTER and membership
Switching to an already granted role does not require GRANT
Explicit regrant is required before selecting the revoked default
Missing roles fail without changing the user
Even ALTER plus GRANT cannot implicitly grant a default role
Switching defaults preserves old grants without granting the executor
CREATE USER plus GRANT can assign a default role
An ordinary password update does not restore a revoked default role
Selecting PUBLIC requires no explicit grant and changes no grants
